      "note": "Cut along the window frame / window contents seam, which is also the seam the three file-scope globals fall on. statwin.c keeps fdps_load_status_cel_image, fdps_draw_status_window_anim_frame and fdps_close_status_window (the artwork, the four-panel slide, the slide run backwards) plus data_fdps_ui_play_active_flag_saved; the one still-pending function routed here, fdps_battle_show_unit_status_window @ 00016aa0, is the window's opening and belongs with them. New statunit.c takes fdps_draw_unit_status_panel, fdps_unit_status_window_wait_input and fdps_draw_unit_inventory plus data_fdps_village_status_window_unit_idx and data_fdps_unit_status_window_last_tick -- the panel drawer writes the village index and the wait loop is its only reader, so they cannot honestly be separated. Dependency is one-way: statwin.c will include statunit.h when the show function lands; statunit.c needs nothing from statwin.h.\n\nLine counts after the cut: src/statwin.c 450 (about 617 once the pending function lands), src/statunit.c 839, both under the 1000 budget. Tests moved with their code: tests/statwin.c 885 lines / 12 cases, new tests/statunit.c 1545 lines / 24 cases, runner renamed to run_statunit_tests. All 36 original cases are present and the whole suite reports 14593 checks, 0 failures.\n\nThree mechanical adjustments were needed beyond a pure move, all verified against the assembly rather than guessed: SCENE_PAGE_*/SCREEN_WINDOW_* were defined in the wait loop's block but also used by the close, so statwin.c carries its own copy with the close's own push addresses (000168fa, 00016932..00016958) rather than the wait loop's; BLIT_MODE_OPAQUE was defined in the load-cel block but used by the wait loop's shadow blit, so statunit.c defines it citing PUSH 0x0 at 00017229 (confirmed from the disassembly of 000170c0); and tests/statunit.c needed <stdio.h> for the FACE.CEL probe that came across with the panel fixture. Per-file duplication of shared VGA/geometry constants is